tour cli-convert
kind layer
author ai
group cli
note convert.rs: the cli crate's values and the conversion from clap's Command into them. A Request is a Query (the reading commands), an Edit (the map edits) or a repin, each variant holding domain values (TourName, TextFragment, SymbolName, RelativePath, Note, GroupName) or the crate's own small types for what the user typed as numbers: StepIndex (a position in the step list, as tours shows it), Under (a parent index where -1 is the root), LineNumber (1-based as typed), Levels (a depth), Count. Conversion never fails: a value that does not validate, such as a tour name with a bad character, is carried as the MapError it produced and reported by exec, so the refusal wording stays in wire.rs. step_id, step_index and line_range are where the user's indices and 1-based lines meet the domain's StepId and 0-based Span.

